# Rolls-Royce Silver Shadow four-door saloon, 1965-1980.
#
# The Silver Shadow: 5,169 mm long, 1,829 mm wide, 1,518 mm high, 3,035 mm
# wheelbase; 6.23-litre V8, hydropneumatic self-levelling suspension, disc
# brakes. The most produced Rolls-Royce of its time (about 16,700 Shadows and
# Shadow IIs) and the class-4 benchmark of the 1970s.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolls-Royce_Silver_Shadow
#
# Colours: Black, Silver, Royal Blue and Burgundy are documented Rolls-Royce
# finishes of the period.
#
# Weight: 25 in total (black 9, silver 7, blue 5, burgundy 4), low per section F
# of the gaps doc.
#
# Speed 190 km/h; comfort 150/555 (line). Classes 3,4.
# Dates: 1965-1980 with a road tail to about 1995.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rolls-royce-silver-shadow.blend. References:
# citycars/references/rolls-royce-silver-shadow/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia
# Commons.

obj=citycar
name=RollsRoyceSilverShadow(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=9
intro_year=1965
intro_month=10
retire_year=1995
retire_month=6
speed=190
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=150
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=555

